From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Le Hoang Quyen <lehoangquyen@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 03:10:48 -0700
Subject: Graphite: Add Delegate interface and handle context loss in readback

Refactor GraphiteSharedContext to use a Delegate interface instead
of individual callback closures, and have DawnSharedContext implement
it. Expose IsContextLost() on GraphiteSharedContext. In
GraphiteImageReadPixels and RasterDecoderImpl::DoReadbackYUVImagePixels,
gracefully handle context loss when readback callbacks are not completed
instead of crashing.

Bug: 537751400
Change-Id: Ib32b99828c7d0c4204d38d5c5d0fe814bdf10320
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8130240
Commit-Queue: Quyen Le <lehoangquyen@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Colin Blundell <blundell@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1666962}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
Picked as a prerequisite for "Skip Graphite async read pixels callback
when context is lost" (cherry-pick-b77d42d0e0c8.patch), which needs
GraphiteSharedContext::Delegate / delegate_. Two context-only conflicts:
the header keeps this branch's existing simulated_insert_status_ member
next to the new delegate_, and dawn_context_provider.cc keeps this
branch's features::kSkiaGraphiteMaxPendingRecordings.Get() accessor
spelling. No semantic changes.

